  "notes": [
    "Segments are the DENOISING path: denoise_step -> paligemma_with_expert.forward with inputs_embeds=[None, suffix] -> gemma_expert.model.forward -> the decoder layer at pi_gemma.py:157-188. compute_layer_complete serves the joint prefix+suffix path and is NOT what a denoising step runs.",
    "embed_suffix returns adarms_cond=None for pi0 (modeling_pi0.py:734), so PiGemmaRMSNorm takes its unconditioned branch and the residuals are plain x+y. pi05 is expected to differ, which is why the branch is recorded per model.",
    "eager_attention_forward calls repeat_kv (modeling_gemma.py:205-206), expanding the single KV head to 8 before both matmuls. Unique KV bytes are counted once in `bytes_host_segment`; the expansion is noted as traffic the analytic model omits.",
    "Inputs are the model's own tensors, captured from one real denoising step of the fixture and replayed; every segment calls the model's own callable where one exists. `partials_residual` and `cast_scores_fp32_fp16` are mapping_only.",
    "2026-09-28 completeness re-run: the 20260924 run never had kernel counts (n_kernels 0 everywhere). This directory is the complete E11a: --mode count (root), --mode nsys (host_sequences), then the timing pass with --kernels-csv. Layer timings reproduce the 20260924 run within 0.5 %. A CPU-only analysis process (bench/e5b_static.py, ncu --import) ran concurrently during the count and nsys passes, not during timing."
  ],
